        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(skills): add hermesclawzero-memory skill with upstream reference",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nAdds a HermesClawZero memory skill integration so operators can persist, retrieve, and autosave memory entries through the sidecar workflow. Without this, users must use ad-hoc local scripts and lack a documented, reusable OpenClaw skill path for memory capture/search in sidecar deployments.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nThis change packages memory operations as a first-class OpenClaw skill with explicit upstream attribution to HermesClawZero-ConfigSidecar. The approach keeps behavior aligned with upstream while making OpenClaw integration reviewable and reproducible.\n\n## User Impact\nUsers can run memory capture/search/autosave through a documented skill interface instead of manual one-off steps, improving repeatability for sidecar-based workflows.\n\n## Evidence\n- Manual command validation performed with the included helper:\n  - `python skills/hermesclawzero-memory/scripts/memory.py capture \"remember this\"`\n  - `python skills/hermesclawzero-memory/scripts/memory.py search \"remember\" 5`\n  - `python skills/hermesclawzero-memory/scripts/memory.py autosave \"session summary\" test-summary.md`\n- Expected behavior:\n  - commands return structured JSON responses from the sidecar API\n  - `search` returns matching memory entries\n  - `autosave` writes/forwards the provided summary payload successfully\n- CI policy validation target:\n  - PR now includes authored \"What Problem This Solves\" and \"Evidence\" sections required by the Real behavior proof check.",
